  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1211 PM MDT Fri May 29 2026\n\nA closed low centered over the Nevada and Utah border will\ninfluence our weather through the weekend. Dry and gusty\nconditions ahead of the system is allowing for critical fire\nweather conditions today, especially in eastern Utah and the\nFour Corners area. In the northern and central Colorado\nmountains lingering moisture will allow for convection this\nafternoon. By this afternoon the center of the low pressure\nsystem will reach eastern Utah, bringing moderate moisture\nadvection and substantial forcing. PoPs increase around 6PM MDT\naround the I-70 corridor, and will gradually move north through\nthe evening. Tonight and tomorrow most of the precipitation is\nexpected to occur in the northern half of our CWA, with PoPs\nfavoring the Uinta Mountains. The moisture advection with this\nlow pressure system will keep critical fire weather conditions \nlocalized after today. \n\nFrontal passage this evening will allow for a drop in high\ntemperatures tomorrow. So, expect tomorrow's highs to be around\n5 to 15 degrees below normal, with the most anomalous\ntemperatures expected north of I-70. Although, a shift to \nwarmer southwesterly flow on Sunday will cause temperatures to\ngradually warm again, and widespread above average temperatures\nreturn by Tuesday.",
